            <ArticleTitle>Management of Peri-Implant Hypertrophic Scarring for an Ear Prosthesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e777-e778</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/SCS.0000000000003976</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clinical report describes a case of a 14-year-old patient with a traumatic amputation of the left auricle and severe hypertrophic scarring. The management of peri-implant soft tissue was challenging, but successful in the rehabilitation of a patient with auricular prosthesis retained by implants. The prosthesis restored the patient's facial aesthetics and contributed not only to function, but also to psychosocial well-being.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
